      "statement": "scripts/next_version.py derives the release bump from Conventional Commit subjects since the last release tag (feat!/BREAKING CHANGE: -> major, feat -> minor, else patch), except that a breaking change on a 0.x version bumps minor instead of major to avoid accidentally declaring API stability; it is shared by the release workflow and `make next-version --explain` so a local preview matches what CI will pick, and it seeds the first release from pyproject.toml's existing version rather than inventing 0.1.0.",
